# Worksheet

**F1 Core loop**: `game` single state object; `createRng`/`initRng` seeded PRNG used via `rngFloat/rngInt/rngChoice/rngShuffle` everywhere; `endTurn()` runs numbered steps 1-9 in fixed order every call. Score 2.

**F2 Map**: 64-tile grid, `getTerrain` derived from seeded `rngFloat` in `initMap`; `canBuild()` checks terrain. BUT: `buildBuilding` is declared twice (top-level), second definition (`buildBuilding.call({}, ...)`) overwrites the first, making the real build logic permanently unreachable — self-recursion instead. Adjacency bonuses (`adjacencyBonus` field) are never read in `getProductionOutput`. Score 1.

**F3 Economy**: `getProductionOutput` consumes/produces per building, caps enforced with overflow log in `endTurn`; water_condenser→greenhouse is a real chain. But buildings can never be placed (see F2 bug), so this pipeline never runs on real data. Score 1.

**F4 Population**: colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job (`addColonist`). `getProductionOutput` reads `colonist.skill` but only via `building.workers`, which is never populated anywhere (no assignment function exists); fatigue never read by production at all. Score 1.

**F5 Needs**: consumption in `endTurn`; shortage lowers morale (`c.morale -= shortage*10`); recovery possible via event effects (`morale_spike`, choices). Morale is never read by `getProductionOutput` — required link missing. Score 1.

**F6 Research**: 12 nodes, `canResearch` enforces prereqs+cost, `doResearch` deducts cost. Only `resilience_1/2` (read in `triggerAshstorm`) and `trade_tech` (read in `endTurn`/`renderTradePanel`) have real effects; 9/12 nodes are cosmetic text only; `population_tech` prereq id (`community_programs`) doesn't match any node id, crashing `canResearch` on every research-tab render. Score 1.

**F7 Events**: 10 `EVENT_DEFINITIONS`; `fireEvent()` uses shuffled deck + cooldown (`eventCooldown`), but no actual weight field; 6 events have 2 choices routed through `applyEventEffects`. `effects.production` branch is empty (no-op); `fired` Set never clears so all events permanently stop firing once each has occurred once. Score 1.

**F8 Trade**: `generateCaravan()` prices via `demandMod` reading `game.resources[res]`; buy/sell both implemented in `trade()`. No hard check `quantity<=offering.quantity` inside `trade()` itself (only UI button-disable enforces it); `globalSupply` never drifts over turns. Score 1.

**F9 Hazard**: `triggerAshstorm()` scales severity with turn, damages buildings, reduced by `storm_shelter`/`resilience` research; `getProductionOutput` scales by damage; `repairBuilding()` spends parts. Entire chain depends on buildings existing, which is blocked by the F2 buildBuilding bug. Score 1.

**F10 Save/load**: `saveGame()` serializes full state to a visible/copyable textarea; `loadGame()` `JSON.parse` in try/catch with `alert` on bad input; round-trip covered by test 9. Score 2.

**F11 End conditions**: `endTurn()` checks `colonists.length===0` (lose) and `turn>=60 && colonists>=12` (win), both reachable; `renderEndScreen` computes score from population/resources/research/turn. Score 2.

**F12 UI**: tab click listener toggles `.active`+`render()`; `addLog` stores `turn`, shown in `renderLogPanel`; keydown handles Space/Digit1-5. `.two-column` responsive class defined in CSS but never applied by any render function — dead. Score 1.

**F13 Dev panel**: `runTests()` has 15 real invariant checks (caps, prereqs, RNG reproducibility, save/load roundtrip); `runBenchmark()` loops `endTurn()` 200x headless and prints `getGameHash()`. Score 2.

**G1**: no research node's stated production bonus (water_tech, metal_tech, food_tech, power_tech, industry_1/2) is ever read in `getProductionOutput`. Score 0.

**G2**: shortage→morale link is real (`c.morale -= shortage*10` every relevant turn), but morale is never read by `getProductionOutput` — final link absent. Score 1.

**G3**: full pipeline exists in source (`triggerAshstorm` sets `building.damage`, `getProductionOutput` scales by it, `repairBuilding` spends parts and resets damage) but is unreachable in practice since buildings can never be created (F2 bug). Score 2.

**G4**: `generateCaravan()` computes `demandMod` from `game.resources[res]`, feeding `pricePerUnit` shown in `renderTradePanel`; no drift over turns, only two discrete demand tiers. Score 3.

**G5**: `resolveChoice()`→`applyEventEffects()` writes different `game.resources`/`game.colonists` changes per branch (checked `supply_shortage`, `disease`); some effect types (`fatigue`, `preparation`) silently dropped in other branches. Score 3.

